WEBVTT

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.730
Wow...

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.640
Seigi, snack time!

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.860
Grandma, is this yours?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.940
It's so pretty.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.020
Why did you put it away? It's pretty.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.160
Seigi, you mustn't do bad things.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.870
You'll pay for them.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.380
<i>The train has temporarily stopped.</i>

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.530
<i>We will be departing shortly.</i>

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.890
Just a dream...

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.860
What's your problem?

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.120
You're the one who tripped.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.260
You're in our way.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.660
Officer!

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.780
Over here! Hurry!

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.790
Someone's being attacked!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.580
Shit! Run!

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.680
Are you all... right...

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.530
A-Are you okay?

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:25.520
Thank you for your help.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.860
<i>That was how I met Richard.</i>

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.950
<u>Episode 1</u>
<b>Seigi of the Pink Sapphire</b>

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.340
Allow me to formally thank you.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.720
Richard Rana...

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.700
Take a look at the back.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.550
My name is Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.310
<b>Jeweler
Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian</b>

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.310
Jewelry Étranger...

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.310
Um, do you appraise jewels? Like on rings?

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:34.320
Yes.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.970
Thank you for today.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.440
Please call me anytime, Mr. Hero of Justice.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.380
Hero of justice, huh?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.810
What did you want to discuss?

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:14.310
Well... You see, I'd like you to appraise a ring.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.570
It seems to be a pink sapphire.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.640
Huh? You can tell just by looking at it?

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.820
To a certain degree.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:26.370
That ring was my grandmother's.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.200
She claimed it was fake,

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.950
but I've always wanted to 
have it appraised by an expert.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.400
But you've never looked into it before now?

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.260
Anyone could've assessed it for you.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:50.090
I know, but I've been busy with exams 
since my grandmother died.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:53.970
Normally, you wouldn't casually 
entrust someone you've just met

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.460
with something so valuable.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.690
If I were a bad person trying 
to take your ring from you,

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.910
you'd never see your precious keepsake again.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.120
What's so funny?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.290
Just that a genuinely bad person 
wouldn't bother telling me that.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.740
I really would like to know about the stone.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.050
Please.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.050
Very well.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.800
Thank you.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.940
The appraising of jewels other than 
diamonds is known as valuating,

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.350
so you've requested a valuation.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.230
<b>Request Form</b>

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.230
Please sign here.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.190
At the soonest, 
the valuation will take a week.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.230
At the latest, 
it could take about a month.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.240
The fee is five thousand yen.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.150
Got it.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.820
Nakata Seigi

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.290
Wow, you even take photos?

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.280
The history of jewels 
is one of fraud and theft.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.430
Theft?

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.140
The consumer and the dealer...

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:06.670
It's an old safety-first tradition 
meant to protect both parties.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.580
I see.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:13.070
Well, then, I'll contact you 
once I have the results.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:22.120
Work your magic.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.480
<b>Takadanobaba Station</b>

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.940
Heya, Nakata!

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.640
Hey, Shimomura.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.160
What's up?

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.750
That old man's here again?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.710
Are you all right?

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.500
Here. Hold my hand.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.540
Um...

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:51.850
Thank you kindly.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.230
Excuse me.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.270
Sir, I'll walk you across.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.850
Please hold firmly on to my hand.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:07.880
Hey!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.320
People may look like they need help,

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.120
but while some are honest, others aren't.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.540
You should be... careful...

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.500
You're right... but how do you tell them apart?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.150
Oh, I haven't thanked you yet.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:32.260
I'm Tanimoto Shoko,
 a second-year education major.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:36.820
I'm Nakata Seigi, 
a second-year economics major.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:40.560
His name means "justice"!
Like a hero of justice!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.030
Shimomura!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.500
You really are a hero of justice.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:45.150
Huh?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.690
Thank you, Seigi-kun.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.060
Don't mention it...

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.580
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.830
The jewel you asked me to take 
a look at is most uncommon.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:10.380
Are you aware that this ring may be stolen?

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:22.890
You're incredible!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.690
You're the real deal!

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.140
Incredible! Truly incredible!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.570
Please quiet down.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.620
I'm sorry for being disingenuous.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.580
Could you explain?

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:44.580
Yes. As you said, this ring was stolen.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.710
My grandmother was a pickpocket.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.540
She was what people call 
a single mother nowadays,

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:57.720
and there was nowhere a woman could
 do honest work while raising a child alone.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.930
She became a pickpocket in order to survive.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.160
But that ring alone...

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:39.470
The next day, the woman who owned 
the ring jumped in front of a train.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.010
My grandmother heard she survived,

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:46.230
and while running home to get 
the ring so she could return it...

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:49.980
She was arrested.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:56.580
My grandmother kept this ring 
until the day she died.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.690
I've always wondered why 
she never got rid of it.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.410
I think she decided that holding on to it

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.590
would be her cross to carry.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:13.420
But this way, my grandmother will 
never be able to rest in peace.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.990
So I investigated the incident by 
looking through old newspapers,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.330
but that turned up nothing.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:25.070
And if I took it to a big store, 
my mother might be notified.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.890
Does your mother not know about the ring?

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:30.900
I'm the only one who does.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:32.520
Hiromi...

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.820
My mother resents my grandmother 
more than anyone.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:41.820
I... I want to end this for her.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.700
If you found out the ring was stolen,

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.910
then that means there's some 
record of a transaction, right?

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.310
Records involving quality items

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:52.420
stick around for a long time, 
even if they're old.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.350
Please. I want you to find 
the original owner of this ring.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.920
I'm determined to return it.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:08.520
There's someone...

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.940
I'd like you to meet in Kobe.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:18.300
<i>And so time that was frozen half a century 
ago in Tokyo began moving with a groan.</i>

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.770
Hiromi, it's me.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:30.040
<i>Don't call your own mother by her name.</i>

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.690
Listen...

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.100
<i>What?</i>

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:35.540
Are you well?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:40.880
<b>Nozomi 187\h\h\h10:30\h\h\hHakata\h\h\hUnreserved Seating: Cars 1-3</b>

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.750
<i>I'm just great.</i>

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.080
That's good.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.440
<i>What is it? I'm about to go out.</i>

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.110
It's about Grandma.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.930
<i>That's none of your business.</i>

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.140
<i>If you don't need anything, I'm hanging up.</i>

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.400
Okay. I'll call back later.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.500
Shall we go?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.360
Yeah.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.450
<b>Shin-Kobe Station</b>

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.680
<b>Miyashita</b>

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.610
Ma'am.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.400
I've been waiting for you, Richard-san.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:49.700
Ma'am, I'm delighted you made 
time to meet me today.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.710
You, too. Come in.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.170
All right.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:00.430
Nice to meet you. I'm Miyashita Tae.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.170
I'm Nakata Seigi.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:06.300
Richard-san told me 
about you over the phone.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.930
You know who I am, don't you?

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:12.600
Yes.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.230
I'd like to return this ring.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:33.380
Before that, would you listen to my story?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:38.240
At the time, I'd just turned twenty.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:40.010
For the sake of my family's debt,

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:43.260
I was to be wed off in a 
marriage of convenience.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:51.140
As far as I was concerned, 
that ring was a collar and chain.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:05.740
I felt as though someone had 
opened the door to my cage.

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:09.160
I wasn't sad in the slightest.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:10.490
What?

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:14.030
My father beat me when I returned home,

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.450
but still, I wasn't sad.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.960
Even I was struck by my 
disobedience to my parents.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:25.080
More so than my entire family's unhappiness 
at the engagement falling through,

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:28.090
I couldn't bear my own unhappiness.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:33.100
I didn't see the point in living anymore.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.490
They said it was a miracle I survived,

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:41.250
but the engagement was called off,

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:45.290
and I was forced into a 
cramped hospital room.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.130
But you know,

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:55.120
the cute doctor with the western accent 
who looked after me there took a liking to me.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.870
You never know what 
life holds in store for you.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.240
Nakata-san.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.940
You should hold on to this.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.920
But my grandmother...

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:17.810
I've never once resented her.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:23.220
In that age, both your grandmother 
and I were powerless.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.070
Could you deliver a message
 to her on my behalf?

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.230
"Thank you."

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.950
"Let go of the burden you've carried
so long and rest in peace."

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:44.210
Nakata-san, please continue
 to help those in need,

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.970
just as you helped Richard-san.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:59.060
I've known Miyashita-sama's 
family for several years.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:04.810
I'd previously asked about the jewel 
from the old woman's unfortunate life.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.360
Then... you knew when you saw the ring?

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.460
At first I wasn't certain,

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:16.210
but according to the specialist 
I asked to valuate it,

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:19.120
the cut matched Miyashita-sama's description.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.900
From the outset, as a padparadscha 
ring from that era in Japan...

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.990
I thought it must be it.

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:27.130
Padparadscha?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:33.340
Sapphires of a distinctive orange-tinted 
pink are called padparadscha.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.700
In Sinhalese, it means "lotus flower."

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.430
If you knew all of that, then why...

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:44.170
Because, at the time, I didn't know 
what your true motive was.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.520
My motive?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:50.690
Yes. It was nothing like what I expected.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.700
I want you to find the 
original owner of this ring.

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:58.840
Stolen goods are typically 
involved in fraud or resale,

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.860
but I couldn't have predicted the 
desires of a foolishly kind person.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:12.400
Yet in the end, I couldn't return it.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.690
She wouldn't accept it.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:20.600
Will... she never forgive her?

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:29.290
Perhaps what your 
grandmother did wasn't right.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:36.110
But I believe she did it to protect 
her precious daughter.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.710
Is that desire not admirable?

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:47.620
The pink sapphire represents
 justice for the weak.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.090
Justice?

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:56.970
Grandma, why do people laugh 
at me for helping those in need?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:59.020
<i>A real hero of justice!</i>

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.620
<i>Goody two-shoes!</i>

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.460
I'm proud of you, Seigi.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:16.680
I believe it's a jewel befitting 
of your grandmother.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.660
You should hold on to it.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.560
Grandma...

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.870
Thank you for today.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:41.970
Take this.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.070
What is it?

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.390
Kansai's most popular pork buns.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.100
What?

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:49.090
I can't accept this.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.980
I'm not insisting that you eat them alone.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.160
Why not return to your parents' home?

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.060
What?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.360
You still have things to discuss.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.480
Probably more than you realize.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.660
Now then, I'll be going.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.380
Hey, Hiromi? I'm coming over today.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.780
<i>Sure, but I don't have anything here.</i>

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:19.880
That's okay.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:25.280
Listen... Was Grandma the one who named me?

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:27.240
<i>Where did that come from?</i>

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.470
Just wondering.

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:32.080
<i>It wasn't just your grandma.</i>

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.200
<i>I thought it was nice, too.</i>

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.350
I see.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.510
Those are the results of my valuation.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:07.990
Thank you.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:12.600
If you'd like, I'd be willing 
to buy that padparadscha.

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:16.860
No, thank you. I have no 
intention of letting that ring go.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.780
I see. I expected as much.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.160
Now, I have another suggestion.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.330
Why don't you work here?

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.170
Me? Work here?

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.660
Yes. I'm planning to open a shop here.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.190
It would only be weekends,

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.980
and you'd only be doing 
odd jobs and cleaning.

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:38.880
What do you think?

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:43.980
Why me? I'm an amateur.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:45.590
I know this is personal,

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:48.320
but my grandmother was from the land
 that produced the padparadscha,

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:50.780
Ratnapura in Sri Lanka.

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:52.740
My grandmother's ring was made

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:55.560
with a gemstone from your 
grandmother's homeland?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:59.520
Yes. It's rather intriguing.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:05.860
A gemstone mined in Sri Lanka was 
polished in Europe and ended up in Japan.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:10.120
The Japanese might say this 
must be some sort of fate.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:13.710
So, what do you say?

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.500
I'd love to!

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:27.140
It's so good! Did you make this?

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:30.540
This is real royal milk tea.

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:33.140
The rest is counterfeit.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:39.420
Come to think of it, this might be 
the first time I've seen you drink

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:40.890
anything but water, Richard-san.

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:45.570
Guests aside, I'm not terribly accustomed

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.900
to being called "Richard-san" 
by my associates.

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:53.260
Then, de... de Vul... d-de Vul...

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.650
Just call me Richard.

00:21:54.650 --> 00:21:56.680
What? No honorific?

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:57.910
It's fine.

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:03.920
Richard it is, then.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.030
I look forward to working with you, Seigi.
